TODO before 1.0 final release


Serious bugs
------------
No known serious bug left so far. Exception raising should be improved.
acos_rn misrounds -0x1.cb3b399d747f3p-55 and -0x1.cb3b399d747f4p-55:
   the shortcut for |x| < 2^-27 has no rounding test.

New functions
-------------
Document the cases on which power is guaranteed correctly rounded values.
Possibly write 2^x and 10^x (in harmonious combination with power)

Proof stuff
-----------
Update chapter asin and write chapter acos. 
   Add the scripts generating the polynomials.
Write Gappa proofs for log2-td, log10-td, expm1, log1p
Check all the existing .gappa against last version of Gappa
 + set the paths right (where there are paths). 
Write proper proofs of the DE integer rounding tests, or remove DE altogether.
The first-step bounds of log.c, asin, acos, asinpi, acospi, sin, cos, tan,
   atan, atanpi, expm1, exp and sinpi_rn were checked rigorously by
   computer in 2026, but these checks are not in this repository and
   have no Gappa proof. The 2^-61.5 bound for |x| >= 0.75 in asin and acos
   is one of them.
The Gappa and LaTeX proof of log is for log-td.c; log.c, which is the
   one compiled, has none.
No second (accurate) step has a complete proof. They are correct only
   if the published lists of worst cases are complete. The list for acos
   on [0.75, 1-2^-13) is not known to be complete.
Prove that sinpi and tanpi need the multiple-precision path only below
   2^-950. This threshold comes from measured errors.
Correct the bounds that the 2026 checks found wrong in docs/latex
   (atan second step: 130 bits, not 136; sinh and cosh; tan; sin).


Cleaning up stuff
-----------------
Check .mpl with underscored variables (some versions of Maple don't like them)
Purge obsolete .mpl
Ensure compilation on icc9 and SunStudio11
Solution: check recent icc first. Then add FMADE macros everywhere FMA intended
add make timings
Remove the left shifts of negative integers in exp-td.c, expm1.c and
   csh_fast.c. They are undefined in C99, but current compilers compile
   them as intended.
Hide the internal functions (scs_*, p_accu, exp13 and others), which
   are exported.
RoundToNearest3 returns inf just below the largest double, and
   scs_get_d rounds subnormal ties away from zero. No function reaches
   these cases.

Autotest stuff
--------------
Add worst cases for all which are currently written TODO
A lot of the  Lefevre worst cases are still missing
Add the CORE-MATH lists of worst cases, with both signs.
You never have enough test cases. In particular asin and acos
More cases around the various boundaries would be welcome.

Optim stuff
-----------
Remove remaining SCS: in atan, in trigo.
Replace the current test for non-IEEE subnormal (on x86) in the code
    with a test taking into account that x86-64 is OK
Minor improvements to atanpi as mentionned in the doc. 
ASINPINOSUBNORMALBOUND (0xa5000000) disables the fast path of asinpi for
   2^-858 <= |x| < 2^-60. The intended 0x0a500000 enables it, but that
   path misrounds hard cases to nearest, so it stays disabled.
Fuse atan-pentium and atan-itanium into atan-de, and add in atanpi. 
Or maybe remove all the DE stuff altogether for cleaning up.

